WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.990
Doctor Strange is finally here to blow our
minds with another mystical side of the Marvel

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.990
universe.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.310
We're introduced to a host of new characters
that inhabit the hidden world of sorcerers

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:13.550
and infinite dimensions, but if all these
new faces have you confused, don't worry.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.140
We're here to help sort it out.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.000
Here's a look at characters in Doctor Strange
who mean more than you realized.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.499
Baron Mordo

00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:25.460
Considering he's Dr. Strange's closest ally
and the Ancient One's top pupil, Karl Mordo's

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.029
sudden heel turn in the post-credits scene
might have come as a surprise to some people.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.849
But it's all part of Marvel's master plan.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:34.640
See, in the comics, Mordo is also Strange's
arch-enemy.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.790
In fact, the plot of the film is based on
a famous storyline that saw Mordo, rather

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:44.400
than Kaecilius, betray the Ancient One in
an attempt to curry favor with Dormammu.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.280
In a way, everything that happens in this
movie is just setting the stage for Mordo's

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.370
villainy in future films.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.530
Wong

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:57.000
As the librarian at Kamar-Taj, Wong is kind
of a strict guy, seemingly incapable of laughter,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.050
but secretly harboring a love of Beyonce.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.310
But you can expect to see a lot more of him
in future films: in the comics, Wong is Doctor

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.400
Strange's steadfast partner and best friend.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.249
We look forward to seeing Wong and Stephen's
friendship blossom in future films—and we

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:13.530
can't wait to see Wong open up more cans of
butt-kicking action with the Kamar-Taj style

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.070
of martial arts.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.729
Nicodemus West

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:21.659
While he wasn't given much screen time, Strange's
colleague and rival Dr. Nicodemus West is

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:23.369
a little more interesting than he seems.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:26.250
"I guess I'll just have to just stick with
Nick."

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.399
"Oh wait a minute.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:28.399
You're not…

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:29.399
You guys aren't."

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:30.399
"What"

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:31.399
"Sleeping together.

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:33.039
Sorry, I thought that was implicit in my disgust."

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:34.670
"Ex, explicit actually."

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:39.270
In the comics, as in the film, he operated
on Strange's hands after his accident, leaving

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.619
them with nerve damage.

00:01:40.619 --> 00:01:45.020
But in the comics, he also later followed
Strange to Kamar-Taj and trained in the magic

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.030
arts as well.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.389
It suggests that there may be more to his
appearance in the movie than we first thought...

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:51.819
Christine Palmer

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:56.799
A surgeon and a former flame to Stephen Strange,
Christine Palmer also has her own long and

00:01:56.799 --> 00:01:58.310
bizarre history in the comics.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.149
She appeared as one of the main characters
in the Night Nurse comics, which also inspired

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:07.069
Rosario Dawson's character in Marvel's line
of Netflix shows, and later even had a romance

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:08.770
with Nightcrawler from the X-Men.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.481
It's fairly certain we won't see Rachel McAdams
appear as Dr. Palmer in any X-Men films, but

00:02:13.481 --> 00:02:17.159
we look forward to seeing her return in future
Doctor Strange adventures.

00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:18.459
Cloak of Levitation

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:22.490
In Doctor Strange, the Cloak of Levitation
is an ancient magical relic with a mind of

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:27.110
its own, choosing to help Strange by protecting
him while he was under attack from Dormammu's

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.110
zealots.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:31.560
In the comics, the Cloak of Levitation was
a gift from the Ancient One, and has even

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.500
helped Doctor Strange save the universe a
time or two.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.980
But while it's powerful, it just doesn't quite
have the same personality that it does in

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.049
the movie.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:40.669
"It likes you."

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.040
Dormammu

00:02:43.049 --> 00:02:44.549
"Dormammu, I've come to bargain!"

00:02:44.549 --> 00:02:47.909
Those are words you'll likely hear a lot from
Doctor Strange fans.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.390
While Strange might have been successful in
annoying the demon lord of the Dark Dimension

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.900
into submission, he didn't actually kill him.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.810
It's also important to note that the bargain
Strange made with Dormammu said that the demon

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.920
would have to leave Earth alone, but it didn't
say anything about Strange leaving the Dark

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.080
Dimension alone.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.489
And since Doctor Strange's one true love in
the comics, Clea, is actually Dormammu's niece

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:11.980
and eventual successor as ruler of the Dark
Dimension, it's a fair bet we'll see Dormammu

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.670
again — and this time, on his terms.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.680
Thanks for watching!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.330
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel and watch more videos like

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.510
the one you just saw.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.219
And don't forget to check out all this cool
stuff we know you'll love, too!

